    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "> You can register a FlopCounterMode formula via HOP.py_impl(FlopCounterMode)\n\n@zou3519 I'm running into this same issue on torch 2.7.1. I have a RoPE triton kernel that I would effectively like to skip counting FLOPS for in both forward and backward but I can't figure out how to use `HigerOrderOperators.py_impl` to disable it\n\nI tried something like below\n\n```\ndef flop_estimator(mode, *args, **kwargs):\n    # Still run the real op\n    return triton_kernel_wrapper_mutation.dispatch(*args, **kwargs)\n\n# Register the implementation\nfoo = triton_kernel_wrapper_mutation.py_impl(FlopCounterMode)\nfoo(flop_estimator)\n```\n\nto try and get it to just call the underlying implementation of the Triton kernel and not do any of the flop counting stuff. But I end up getting `assert isinstance(k, DispatchKey)`. This seems to come from the `py_impl` of `OperatorBase` which effectively checks `issubclass(FlopCounterMode, TorchDispatchMode)` which rather suprisingly returns False (some metaclass business is breaking issubclass)\n\n",
